<title>USA: AGA says U.S. weekly natgas stocks fell 147 bcf.</title>
<headline>AGA says U.S. weekly natgas stocks fell 147 bcf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Gas Association estimates of U.S. working gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):		    02/14/97  02/07/97  Net Chg  Pct Full(6)</p>
<p> Producing Reg. (1)	  252     288	-36     28</p>
<p> Consuming Reg. East (2)   687     784	-97     38</p>
<p> Consuming Reg. West (3)   188     202	-14     39</p>
<p> Total U.S.		   1127    1274     -147     35</p>
<p>Notes: (1) Incl Texas, Okla., Kansas, N.Mexico, Arkansas, Louisiana, and Miss. (2) Incl states east of Miss. River less Miss., plus Iowa, Neb and Missouri (3) Incl states west of the Miss. River less producing region and Iowa, Neb and Missouri.  </p>
<p>Survey sample and full working gas estimates</p>
<p> -			 Survey Sample   Est. Full Work-    Yr-Ago</p>
<p> -			 Size--Pct (4)   ing Gas--BCF (5)   Week</p>
<p> Producing Region	    71		    908	   270</p>
<p> Consuming Region East     94		   1790	   454</p>
<p> Consuming Region West     96		    482	   260</p>
<p> Total U.S.		    88		   3180	   984</p>
<p>Notes: (4) Ratio of max WG vol. to est. of highest WG in storage in past 2 yrs (EIA).(5) Highest WG level by state added to give regional and national levels (EIA).(6) Regional and total vols divided by est.full regional and total vols.</p>
</text>
